payload.text:
The "White Screen" is happening because the code is mixing two different versions of Firebase. The `index.html` is loading the **new** version (v12 Modular), but the code is trying to use the **old** commands (v8 Namespaced). This causes the app to crash immediately because the old commands don't exist in the new library.

To fix the loop and the crash, I will **strictly update everything to the modern Modular Syntax** (v9+). This is the correct way to use Firebase in 2025.

### Instructions to fix Database Permissions (Firestore Rules)
If you didn't set "Test Mode," your database is likely blocking all writes.
1. Go to the **Firebase Console** (console.firebase.google.com).
2. Click **Build** > **Firestore Database**.
3. Click the **Rules** tab.
4. Change the code to allow authenticated users to read/write:
   ```
   rules_version = '2';
   service cloud.firestore {
     match /databases/{database}/documents {
       match /{document=**} {
         allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
       }
     }
   }
   ```
5. Click **Publish**.

Here are the code updates to fix the White Screen:

